--- The math constructors and distributions are rows of the builtin table
--- (docs/bug-classes.md §4): one runtime function checks each size and
--- parameter, for both modes. zeros[-2] stopped the interpreter with its
--- reason and panicked the compiled program ("capacity overflow"), eye[-1]
--- overflowed a multiplication there, and a distribution's bad parameter
--- panicked both.
use math
log[len[zeros[2, 3]]]
log[ones[2]]
log[eye[2]]
log[full[2, 7.5]]
log[linspace[0, 1, 3]]
log[arange[0, 1, 0.25]]
log[diag[[1, 2]]]
seed[7]
log[len[poisson[2.0, 5]]]
log[len[normal[0, 1, 3]]]
n = len[[1, 2]] - 3
log[zeros[n]]
log['not reached']
